  "description": "Calculate between-group variance, within-group variance, and F-ratio test statistic across multiple sample groups.\n\nOne-way ANOVA partitions total sum of squares into explainable between-treatment variance and residual within-treatment error variance.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\nF = \\frac{\\text{MSB}}{\\text{MSW}} = \\frac{\\text{SSB} / (k - 1)}{\\text{SSW} / (N - k)}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Compute grand mean across all combined group observations\n2. Calculate between-group sum of squares SSB and degrees of freedom k - 1\n3. Calculate within-group sum of squares SSW and evaluate F-statistic MSB / MSW\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'f_statistic', 'ms_between', 'ms_within', 'df_between', and 'df_within'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: ANOVA F-Statistic\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nReal-world data is inherently noisy and uncertain. Probability theory and statistics provide principled tools to quantify that uncertainty, model how data is generated, and evaluate confidence in empirical results. **ANOVA F-Statistic** evaluates probability distributions or statistical tests to summarize sample characteristics.\n\nOne-way ANOVA partitions total sum of squares into explainable between-treatment variance and residual within-treatment error variance. In this problem, the goal is to: calculate between-group variance, within-group variance, and f-ratio test statistic across multiple sample groups.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\nF = \\frac{\\text{MSB}}{\\text{MSW}} = \\frac{\\text{SSB} / (k - 1)}{\\text{SSW} / (N - k)}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Compute grand mean across all combined group observations\n2. **Phase 2**: Calculate between-group sum of squares SSB and degrees of freedom k - 1\n3. **Phase 3**: Calculate within-group sum of squares SSW and evaluate F-statistic MSB / MSW\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Statistical Significance**: Machine learning A/B testing and model evaluation rely on p-values and confidence intervals to ensure observed improvements are not just random noise.\n* **Tail Probabilities & Underflow**: In deep generative models or Bayesian inference, computing log-probabilities prevents underflow when dealing with very small probability values in distribution tails.\n* **Moments & Distributions**: Examining mean, variance, skewness, and kurtosis helps data practitioners detect outliers and choose appropriate normalization strategies.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: groups = [[82, 93, 61, 74], [96, 90, 85, 89], [70, 72, 68, 75]]\n\nOutput: {\"f_statistic\": 5.1775, \"ms_between\": 364.5833, \"ms_within\": 70.4167, \"df_between\": 2, \"df_within\": 9}\n\nExplanation: Evaluated probstat_anova_f_test under standard test conditions."
