  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef probstat_anova_f_test(groups: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **ANOVA F-Statistic** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef probstat_anova_f_test(groups: list) -> dict:\n    all_v = np.concatenate([np.array(g, dtype=float) for g in groups])\n    gm = np.mean(all_v)\n    ssb = sum(len(g) * ((np.mean(g) - gm)**2) for g in groups)\n    ssw = sum(sum((x - np.mean(g))**2 for x in g) for g in groups)\n    df_b, df_w = len(groups) - 1, len(all_v) - len(groups)\n    msb, msw = ssb / df_b, ssw / df_w\n    return {'f_statistic': round(float(msb / msw), 4), 'ms_between': round(float(msb), 4), 'ms_within': round(float(msw), 4), 'df_between': df_b, 'df_within': df_w}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
